id: pm-ado-ntkc
title: Read a project through the work item batch endpoint instead of one request per item
description: "The batch endpoint accepts up to two hundred sub-requests in a single call. A project sync that issues one request per work item is the difference between a handful of round trips and hundreds, which for an agent is latency and token budget rather than an abstract efficiency concern. Batching also keeps the sync inside the service rate limits on projects large enough to matter."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "area:performance"
created_at: "2026-09-02T18:06:06.392Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T15:49:08.016Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T15:43:52.123Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T15:43:52.123Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: A sync of more than two hundred items issues ceiling of n over two hundred batch calls and no per-item reads; the request count is asserted by test rather than assumed; a partial batch failure is surfaced per sub-request rather than failing the whole sync
parent: pm-ado-g4v1
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T15:43:22.190Z",pi-agent,"Verified BATCH_LIMIT=200 against the Azure DevOps REST API 7.1 docs (Maximum 200). Added errorPolicy: 'omit' to the batch request so a missing work item does not fail the whole batch call. Added getWorkItemsReport method that returns { items, missing } surfacing per-item failures rather than silently dropping them. getWorkItems preserves its existing return shape (AdoWorkItem[]) by delegating to getWorkItemsReport. Verified: partial batch failure test asserts missing ids are surfaced, request body includes errorPolicy:'omit', and the test fails when the guard is reverted. 129 tests pass, 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-09-08T15:49:08.016Z",claude-orchestrator,"Batch read retained as implemented: POST _apis/wit/workitemsbatch with errorPolicy omit, chunked at BATCH_LIMIT=200, plus getWorkItemsReport returning items and missing so a dropped id is surfaced rather than silently absent. getWorkItems keeps its existing AdoWorkItem[] shape. Unchanged by the concurrency correction."
close_reason: "Done: errorPolicy:omit added to batch request; getWorkItemsReport surfaces missing items per sub-request; getWorkItems preserves existing return shape. Verified BATCH_LIMIT=200 against API 7.1 docs. 129 tests, 100/100/100/100 coverage, all gates pass."
body: ""
